  "foaf:name": "Autonomous samplers and sensors for marine ‘omics",
  "sdo:name": "Autonomous samplers and sensors for marine ‘omics",
  "sdo:description": "TechOmics is a programme to design and develop autonomous deployable biomolecular sensors and samplers to map and understand marine life. Technology can only be developed through sustained funding and thus our programme is as diverse as the many leveraged projects that fund it. Research in our team ranges from deep sea biodiversity to marine microbiology and biogeochemistry, and target assays for sensors are primarily developed to understand water borne threats to human health such as harmful algae.",
